om/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T01:40:28-07:00","id":94792,"title":"","content":"I do prefer daredevils to be something more than ordinary. It does help suspension of disbelief for me that there is a reason these people can continually flout probability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T07:30:31-07:00","id":94922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/8447-paramorphs-is-there-a-decision-already?p=94792#post94792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do prefer daredevils to be something more than ordinary. It does help suspension of disbelief for me that there is a reason these people can continually flout probability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same reason I prefer paramorphs and daredevils to be the same thing on some spectrum of things, aye.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T08:15:01-07:00","id":94947,"title":"","content":"I ran into this last week recently when running Adventure! 2/3rds of my group are Daredevils. They register as normal to the Psychic Knack, Telluric Resonance. If the 1 other PC gets singled out for the spotlight every time this Knack is used, it makes the other characters feel like they made a sub-optimal choice. That's no fun. I quickly House Ruled that the Knack shows all types of Inspired. Ditto for the Dynamic Knack, Aetheric Vision.<br /> <br /> Unlike most people here, I'm just running the Adventure! portion of Trinity. I'm using it b/c I like the Storyteller systems as the right blend of crunchy and chewy mechanics. The Knacks simulate the &quot;feel&quot; of Pulp much, much better than anything else I've run across or tried to create in other systems.<br /> <br /> Almost everything I've read in this forum relegates the Adventure era to how it fits in with the Aberrant and Aeon era paradigms. When I'm thinking about it, I'm coming from the opposite direction: How would Aberrant and Aeon fit into my Inspired universe?<br /> <br /> I keep an eye on this forum while I'm running Adventure!, but unfortunately for me so little is applicable to my game. If anyone has more Adventure! thoughts, I encourage you to share. I'm listening for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Jason, the Storyteller<br /> -<br /> &quot;Old dreams become new again in the spring. This is where the nightmares are.&quot;</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1357-storyteller31","name":"Storyteller31","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T09:26:43-07:00","id":94995,"title":"","content":"It honestly took us a while in design, but there's a pretty curious middle ground between &quot;these are ordinary humans&quot; and &quot;capable of incredible deeds of heroism - literally not credible deeds&quot; that actually allows you to fulfill both conditions. Everybody wins!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T10:15:27-07:00","id":95021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/8447-paramorphs-is-there-a-decision-already?p=94995#post94995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It honestly took us a while in design, but there's a pretty curious middle ground between &quot;these are ordinary humans&quot; and &quot;capable of incredible deeds of heroism - literally not credible deeds&quot; that actually allows you to fulfill both conditions. Everybody wins!</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the reasons I like Adventure! so much. Storyteller31, I've been running an Adventure!/Aberrant/Trinity game for a few years now, so I've got a few ideas for you (after I get back from lunch).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T18:18:43-07:00","id":111150,"title":"","content":"Been lurking for a bit and talking to my friends about revival of this amazing Series.<br /> <br /> So i thought I\u2019d throw my 2 cents in because i have always been a big fan of the daredevils from adventure, and how they evolved into paramorphs.<br /> <br /> I understand that &quot;canonically&quot; only Maxwell was a paramorph, much like how Dr Primoris. was a nova in the age of stalwarts. Maybe cause they took the Hammersmith incident in the face. and all, but i don't think that should limit anyone.. just cuz they took it in the face just means they got more of the telluric energy than the average person.<br /> <br /> Of course it made those 2 characters Unique and important,<br /> <br /> But for me, I have always seen Daredevils/paramorphs as the evolutionary &quot; I give 0 f*cks&quot; type... Smoking a Cigar while pouring jet fuel,<br /> <br /> and My own old Daredevil Character, had a Unique Knack, a Simple probability Knack, &quot; he always walked out of the shadows&quot; in broad daylight a cloud would block out the sun long enough for him to come onto scene, or that shadowy alley way.<br /> it was just a unique Cinematic knack, but it was a unique knack to him.<br /> <br /> another thing that made daredevils unique, and There was never really any reason given, in adventure, there was no real reason, why, a Daradevil/paramorph, wouldn't be able to get cross knacks, like having a few heroic knacks, or the occasional psy-knack. all be it at higher costs maybe.<br /> <br /> I would assume a paramoprh, would be that guy, that looks at a Nova and smiles and says &quot; oh you think your a God, that's cool, good luck with that&quot; and then walk over to a psion and &quot;hey that's a really cool thing you can do with your mind&quot; But then just walk away unimpressed.<br /> <br /> But maybe that's just me<br /> <br /> in short, i always saw them as the &quot;unique&quot; every-men.<br /> <br /> Where as a Nova bends Reality to it's Will, and a psion bends reality to his mind. to a paramorph, Realty bends to their presence alone.<br /> <br /> Nova's say, &quot; i want THIS to happen!&quot; a psion says &quot;This should happen.&quot; and a paramorph says &quot;Is that not suppose to happen?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2703,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2703-xalzamir","user":"xalzamir","date":". 04-11-2014, 10:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2703-xalzamir","name":"xalzamir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T00:04:56-07:00","id":111321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xalzamir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/8447-paramorphs-is-there-a-decision-already?p=111150#post111150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nova's say, &quot; i want THIS to happen!&quot; a psion says &quot;This should happen.&quot; and a paramorph says &quot;Is that not suppose to happen?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fun way to put it. I like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T02:20:14-07:00","id":129737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xalzamir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/8447-paramorphs-is-there-a-decision-already?p=111150#post111150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nova's say, &quot; i want THIS to happen!&quot; a psion says &quot;This should happen.&quot; and a paramorph says &quot;Is that not suppose to happen?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha! Yeah, that's pretty good.<br /> <br /> Speaking only for the original setting, a daredevil and a paramorph are two different things. My design concept on daredevils was that they're Indiana Jones or Jack Burton types \u2014 normal humans, yes, but special in a narrative sense. This was translated into Knacks due to the necessities of game mechanics, so that there was a simple, central rules system governing all character types.<br /> <br /> I appreciate how some people may think that makes daredevils unique compared to, say, mesmerists. And, to a certain extent, they're right. But then again, mesmerists are just as unique \u2014 they have kick-ass mental powers! The game mechanics exist simply to support different character types so that players can choose the one they think will be most fun to play. Each character type is special in its own way.<br /> <br /> (And hello, Trinity Continuum folks! Only just discovered the forum; great to see the continued interest in these games.)<br /> <br /> Bates","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2959-bates","name":"Bates","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2959_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T15:03:04-07:00","id":130287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bates</strong> <a h